WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.702
-Our next guest is
a very funny comedian

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.105
you know from his show
"Joe Pera Talks With You."

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.408
Tickets for his "Summer in
the Midwest and Rust Belt" tour

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.577
as well as his
"Fall Everywhere Else" tour

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:14.046
are available on joepera.com.

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:17.016
Please welcome back to the show
our friend, Joe Pera, everybody!

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:18.885
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:25.758 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:32.331 align:start size:34% position:66% line:0%
♪♪

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.233
-Welcome back to the show, Joe.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:36.702
-It's crazy to be here tonight,

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.238
on the same night as
Katie Holmes.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.241
'Cause my name's Joe

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:44.877
and she played Joey on
"Dawson's Creek."

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.547
Also, Joe Biden
is our president.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:48.615
-What?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.650
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.420
That's a --
yeah, that's a real,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.722
real curiosity.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.692
I'm so excited you're
going on this stand-up tour.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.893
And I'm curious,

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.795
when you get ready for
a big tour like this,

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.997
are you doing a
lot of stand-up to prepare?

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:09.468
-Yeah, doing shows all over
to warm up.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:13.239
I actually did an anime
convention last weekend.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:17.043
I was pretty nervous,
but it went well

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.312
'cause I opened with the joke,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:23.015
"I'm so excited to be performing
at this anime convention

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:25.184
that I could scream."

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.587
Aarrggghhh!

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.861
Like an anime guy.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.029
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.964
-Did they -- I mean,
I'm assuming there --

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.800
I mean, they must have
just lost their minds.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.136
-They went nuts.

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:46.906
I said, "Sorry,
I can't go Super Saiyan for you,

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.240
but that's the best I can do."

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.775
-I'm sure they were
plenty happy.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.911
Hey, I'm glad you're
going on tour again

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.079
because I'm such a fan of yours.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:54.747
I am so sorry
"The Joe Pera Talks to You,"

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.049
a wonderful show,
it is not coming back.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:59.618
-No, after three seasons,
they pulled the plug.

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:01.988
Was definitely a bummer.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.023
But my friend
Carmen Christopher...

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:05.057
-Yeah
-...you know him --

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.626
he sent me a Steve Harvey clip

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:10.662
off of one of those
alpha Instagram pages.

00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:13.132
And Steve Harvey said,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:17.303
"If a door closes,
don't bang on it,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.272
because if you turn around,

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.674
the hallway of life
will present other doors.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.543
And if you're banging
on that one door,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.545
you can't go down
and see other doors."

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:28.381
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:34.487
-That's, uh -- That will be
a hard line to forget.

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.489
-It did cheer me up.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:37.790
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.993
-Do you have
anything else lined up

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.528
with the open time
you have now?

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:47.266
-Oh, that's why -- Yeah,
I'm really excited to tell you

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.935
that Carmen and Steve's advice

00:02:49.935 --> 00:02:51.237
was really important

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:57.009
because just the following week,
I got a phone call.

00:02:57.009 --> 00:03:02.048
They asked me to be
the next James Bond.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.315
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:05.317
-You're going to be
the new James Bond?

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:08.453
-They needed a different angle
after Daniel Craig,

00:03:08.453 --> 00:03:10.156
and now they decided,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:14.026
"Why not a celibate
American James Bond?"

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.261
-Uh-huh.

00:03:16.261 --> 00:03:18.097
Now, are you --

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.132
I have a lot of
questions about this,

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.568
but, um, how do you feel,

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:23.869
you know,
because this is, of course,

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:29.942
as iconic a British character
in fiction there is.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.711
Do you --
How are British audiences

00:03:32.711 --> 00:03:34.147
responding to this news?

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:37.083
-I, well, this is
the new -- this is --

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.251
They'll be finding out
from this show, I think.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:40.486
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.154
-I think they're
going to love it.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:44.390
It's also --
the new angle they're taking

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.661
that James Bond
lives in Philadelphia,

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.397
he eats prewrapped
Boar's Head sandwiches

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:54.333
for breakfast and lunch,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:58.171
he's learning to play
the guitar off of YouTube,

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:02.541
and he's very afraid of dogs.
-Okay.

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:06.312
This seems like a really big
departure, not just in casting,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.648
but, you know,
James Bond's whole thing.

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:15.321
-I give them a lot of credit
for trying to refresh this.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.055
-Yeah, you know.
You know what? You're right.

00:04:17.055 --> 00:04:18.691
I'm sitting here
congratulating you

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.459
when we should be giving
them a lot of credit.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.862
They're the ones putting
their necks on the line.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.963
-They're taking a risk.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:25.598
But I think, I don't know,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:28.568
I don't see how it doesn't
work out for everybody.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:31.237
-Have you done a --
have you shot anything yet?

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.839
-It's funny you ask,
because we actually --

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.475
yeah, they wanted me
to show the first clip.

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:37.610
-Oh, great.
-Yep.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.645
-From...
-So, is this like a teaser clip?

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:42.515
-Yeah, it was very
early on in filming.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.484
-Okay.
-Yeah, this is --

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:46.252
Hopefully, it doesn't
give too much away.

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:48.654
But this is from the --

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:50.422
James Bond is on his
first mission.

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:55.028
-Okay. And what --
that's all we need to know?

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:57.096
-Pretty much.
-Okay.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:58.230
Let's take a look.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.533
This is, I guess,
the first look at Joe Pera

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:02.702
as the new James Bond.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.104
Here's a clip of him
on his first mission.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.349 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.220
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.858
So I, again,

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:28.861
I end up with more questions
than answers, I feel like.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.263
But -- So it seemed like that
started with a man

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.299
spitting out...

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.935
-Yeah, yeah, we were shooting,

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:41.774
and he just pulled right into
the camera and spit something.

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:45.912
And, you know, sometimes
the part of filmmaking

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.547
is embracing imperfections,

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:49.048
so we decided to keep it in.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.416
-Wow.
-Yeah, so part of

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:54.687
the new angle of
the new James Bond, too.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.490
-So, it seems like --
I, like -- I've always pictured

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:00.459
a James Bond set as really being
locked down and, you know,

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:03.996
not being a situation
where a guy could just sort of

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.498
drive through the shot.

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:09.635
-We've actually put an ad on
Craigslist that says,

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.603
"Drive through
if you feel like it."

00:06:11.603 --> 00:06:13.439
-Oh.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:16.075
That's good.

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.142
You have any more?

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:18.377
I mean, I think, like,

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:21.246
obviously, the appetite is
whetted here, but...

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:23.649
-Yeah, this is another one

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.818
from kind of
the middle of the movie.

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.853
It might be hard to figure out
what's going on.

00:06:27.853 --> 00:06:30.256
But I think --
I think you'll --

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.191
I think it will make
sense once you play it.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.193
-Okay.
Let's take a look at another

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.396
scene from the new "James Bond."

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.478
-So, what's --
what was --

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:55.281
I, um, I don't know
what's going on.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:59.184
-This is a scene from when
James gets pissed off

00:06:59.184 --> 00:07:03.322
that people are littering
faster than he can pick it up.

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:04.523
-I see, yeah.

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.291
And he seems like
a broken man in the end.

00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:07.493
Because he ends up --

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.895
he ends up littering
with the bag of litter.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.464
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.131
So this is sort of
the "hero is lost"

00:07:13.131 --> 00:07:14.433
type moment that happens.

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:15.701
Usually around the end of Act 2.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.736
-Right, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:19.138
-And I don't --
-What's the name?

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.741
They always have names like
"Quantum of Solace."

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:23.443
Does this have a title yet?

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:26.445
-The working title is
"James Bond!"

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:30.783
with an exclamation point
afterward.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.852
-To let people know
it's a little more exciting

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:36.121
than the James Bond
you're used to.

00:07:36.121 --> 00:07:37.723
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:39.658
-And then, yeah, I don't want to
spoil the ending,

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:44.197
but this is the final --
-Final scene?

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:48.267
I feel like that will
spoil the ending.

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:50.937
-Well, I don't know.
I don't know.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.705
Do you guys
want to see the ending scene?

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.941
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:59.545
-All right, here's the --
You want to tell us

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.781
afterwards
what we're supposed to see?

00:08:01.781 --> 00:08:04.149
-No, just that I actually
heard that they're putting

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:05.851
the full plots in trailers now,

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:08.287
just so that people want to know
what they're seeing.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:09.222
-Right.

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:12.157
-So MGM can't be too pissed off.

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:13.092
-Okay, great.

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:14.059
Let's take a look
at the last scene

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:15.928
from the new James Bond movie.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:24.303
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.372
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:35.147
-So -- the writers -- I wasn't
going to do it at first,

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:38.050
but then the writers said that
there was character development

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.519
shown by, in the end, he decides

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:43.789
that he wants to get
chicken, rice, and beans

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:46.391
from a lunch takeout
down the street

00:08:46.391 --> 00:08:49.595
as opposed to eating
a prepackaged sandwich again.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:50.662
-Oh, I see.

00:08:50.662 --> 00:08:51.863
-And then -- Yep.

00:08:51.863 --> 00:08:53.666
-it's neat to see him
in a baseball hat.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:57.169
I feel like you almost never
see James Bond,

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.470
any of the previous
James Bond --

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.739
Did you have a favorite actor,
before you, obviously --

00:09:00.739 --> 00:09:03.042
Did you have a favorite actor
who played James Bond?

00:09:04.342 --> 00:09:05.845
-They are all so good.

00:09:05.845 --> 00:09:06.879
-Yeah.

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:08.214
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:11.483
How about -- There's so many,
you know --

00:09:11.483 --> 00:09:13.986
At this point, I don't know if
you can call them catchphrases,

00:09:13.986 --> 00:09:17.155
but there's certainly a way
James Bond talks.

00:09:17.155 --> 00:09:21.193
You know, all the clips
were sort of absent of dialogue.

00:09:21.193 --> 00:09:23.662
Do you, in the body of this,
do you actually speak

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:26.065
and have some of those
James Bondy-type lines?

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:30.970
-Yep. We're working on some of
the classic lines right now.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:33.338
Everybody knows some of them,
but yeah.

00:09:33.338 --> 00:09:36.608
I was doing --
working on the one scene

00:09:36.608 --> 00:09:40.178
where I do the big line,
and figured --

00:09:40.178 --> 00:09:41.814
Do you want to read it with me?

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:42.881
-The scene with you?
-Yeah.

00:09:42.881 --> 00:09:45.650
-Yeah, okay, sure.
So who am I?

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:49.121
Oh, I'm a -- So can I assume --
Oh, yeah, I'm Bartender.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.423
-Yep.
-Oh, this makes sense,

00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:52.191
'cause I think we all know
the iconic line

00:09:52.191 --> 00:09:53.559
we're working towards.
-Yes.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:54.960
-'Cause he has
a certain kind of --

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.362
I don't need to tell you guys.
There's a certain drink.

00:09:57.362 --> 00:09:58.631
Alright. Can I read it?
-Yep.

00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:00.299
-Okay, here we go.

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:01.867
Here is your IPA.

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:03.603
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:06.172
What is your name?

00:10:07.806 --> 00:10:09.341
-My name is James Bond.

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:11.277
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.082
What is your name?

00:10:18.183 --> 00:10:20.452
-[ Chuckles ]

00:10:20.452 --> 00:10:23.188
Pete Buttigieg.

00:10:23.188 --> 00:10:25.257
I'm the Secretary
of Transportation.

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:30.695
-What are you doing
in Philadelphia?

00:10:30.695 --> 00:10:32.932
-Oh, just hanging out.

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:39.404
-I've actually been hoping to
see you to tell you my idea.

00:10:39.404 --> 00:10:42.341
You should do
a high-speed rail nationwide.

00:10:42.341 --> 00:10:46.211
-That is a good idea.
But how fast should it go?

00:10:46.211 --> 00:10:47.913
-1,000.

00:10:50.049 --> 00:10:51.217
-Joe.

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.119
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.119 --> 00:10:54.286
I'm --

00:10:54.286 --> 00:10:57.556
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:01.594 --> 00:11:04.330
Not until this moment
have I felt this,

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:05.563
but I'm starting to get
a little worried

00:11:05.563 --> 00:11:07.265
about the new James Bond.

00:11:07.265 --> 00:11:10.002
[ Laughs ]

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:12.070
-The only way that it could fail

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:15.707
is that we don't get Pete
to play himself.

00:11:15.707 --> 00:11:18.377
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, that scene would be weird

00:11:18.377 --> 00:11:20.546
if you don't get
the actual Pete Buttigieg.

00:11:20.546 --> 00:11:22.648
Like an actor
playing Pete Buttigieg.

00:11:22.648 --> 00:11:24.483
-It wouldn't --
It wouldn't quite sell it.

00:11:24.483 --> 00:11:27.520
-Yeah, that's pretty much
the only problem.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:32.724
So you shot the three scenes you
brought, and you're rehearsing

00:11:32.724 --> 00:11:34.026
for this scene.
-Yep.

00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:36.028
-But you don't know
if you have Pete Buttigieg.

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.462
-Nope.

00:11:37.462 --> 00:11:40.266
-What's the budget
for this movie?

00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:41.299
-Mm...

00:11:41.299 --> 00:11:44.102
-About 1,000?
[ Laughs ]

00:11:44.102 --> 00:11:46.505
-Part of the reason we're going
to try and get Pete

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:48.774
Is that he might divert
some of the funds

00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:53.145
from the Transportation
Department

00:11:53.145 --> 00:11:54.980
in the James Bond movie.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:57.049
-See, I'm always worried you
haven't thought this through,

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:59.518
and you always have.

00:11:59.518 --> 00:12:00.986
Joe, it's always
a pleasure to have you.

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:02.855
Congratulations again on
this James Bond move.

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:04.423
Thank you so much
for sharing it with us.

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:05.691
Joe Pera, everybody!

00:12:05.691 --> 00:12:07.826
For tickets
to his upcoming tours,

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:09.361
visit joepera.com.

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:10.629
Tickets are still available

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:12.964
for Meyer Theater
in Green Bay, Wisconsin,

00:12:12.964 --> 00:12:14.166
on August 26th.

00:12:14.166 --> 00:12:15.735
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

